for all these people claming the game is broken there is a simple fix that i will post in this comment because i got the cant find steam problem and when i did this it worked just fine and it saves u all are welcome in the future:)
If the config tool fails to launch with a "Can't find Steam" error message, simply restarting Steam should fix that.
If the issue persists or the config tool freezes at one point while gathering system information on your first launch, try the following;
Locate the JadeEmpireConfig file in the game's Steam folder (usually found at C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Jade Empire)
Right click, select properties, select compatibility and set it to compatibility mode for Windows Vista SP2.
If this fails to fix the freeze, you must do the following;
Using notepad, create a blank text file.
Name it SystemInformation.xml and save it in the data folder inside the Jade Empire folder (usually found at C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Jade Empire\data).
Copy the Steam.dll file from the base Steam folder (C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam) and paste it into the Jade Empire folder (C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Jade Empire - NOT the data folder).
Information This will effectively bypass the config tool which should allow you to launch the game.

(Review writed with 7.6 hours gaming and all achievements unlocked - Jan 01st, 2017).
Out There Somewhere is a 8-bit portal game with a little of space invaders. You play with a space pilot who's crashlanded on an alien world, and you've found yourself inside a retro-tinged platformer in which each room works as a single puzzle, all to repair your spaceship.
Pros:
- Challenging puzzles;
- Nice 8-bit portal game play.
Cons:
- Few levels;
- Lame history;
- Few boring challenges;
- Hard achievements.
6,0/10.

