/// R E V I E W \\\
So, you came here for a review. Here it is.
/// B R I E F  P L O T \\\
Jesse, your protaganist, starts out in a little tree house in the middle of no where, (with friends.) As he/she continues their journey to 'Endercon', they find out their are many dangers they have to face. They end up making a deal with a shady character, roaming to try to trade them a treasure, but little did Jesse know, this man was very dishonest. This shady character disapears off, to finish off their creation to destroy the world. The shady character eventually makes and brings the evil creature to destruct all of Minecraft. With Jesse's group being the only brave civilians around, the monster that lurks has to be stopped. An old member of 'The Order of the Stone' is desperate for help, as he fights off the scary beast. Jesse and his friends try their best to help out, but some are seperated... that's up to you. The group venture off to find the rest of to find the rest of 'The Order of the Stone' to reunite them, and save the world from mass destruction. Will they fail? Will they be successful with their quest? It's up to you!

/// G A M E  P R O S \\\
This game is probaly one of the first kid freindly games I have seen from Telltale. I also like the fact that they mixed one of the most dominating games in children history with one of the most popular games series "creators" . The graphics are, well, blocky! It also features the some of the minecraft texture that whom know of. In my opinion this game is great and I love it so far.
But there are some things I want to point out, so. Hold onto your wallets!
/// G A M E  C O N S \\\
Some of the voice acting cuts off in mid sentence later episode 3 and above, specificaly for male Jesse. It can be kind of annoying at times but if you keep your subtitles on like me it shouldn't be a huge problem. Another problem with "tan" male Jesse. Near the end to episode 3 your character Jesse... starts to look like a girl. But I won't go into "too" much detail.
There isn't much freedom like in minecraft. You occasionly get to build but all you really do is press "q or e" over and over to build and you dont build in first person, if you have seen the trailers/played or seen Telltale games, you'll understand. You also continue having to use the same keys in different situations which I will try not to mention.
A little update on the cons, I have now found a story rich series which I like alot and is very good. Add a few good animations/good acting, good voice acting, a great plot, good drama and bam, you have a very good movie/series/video/game. I've just kept on wanting more of this series. This now that I think of it isn't as good as I first saw it. Although I still, love this game.
/// R E V I E W  E N D \\\
Over all it is a pretty good game. Love it. t's a 6/10 from me!
