/// D I S C L A I M E R \\\
This is mostly about Minecraft: Story Mode, episode 6-8.  (8 is mostly mentioned)
/// U P D A T E \\\
Thought I might as well update my review, as more episodes have come out and the game has changed alot.
/// G A M E  P R O S \\\
Well, now that there has been quite a big change in story, I can say (without spoiling anything) I still like the game as I did before.
My opinion aside, I saw quite an improvement in the storyline with more variety, (breif spoilers: with the portals making more "variety", with more worlds to explore etc.) more characters introduced, and more. I enjoy more quirky characters for the game, and I can't believe it came from a trio, to dozens of characters that are.. memorable(?). I can't say it was something I'd stay with for long, I mean I stuck with the series in the first couple of episodes, but I stopped playing after a bit, due to having to pay for the next few episodes (which I will mention later in the game cons). I don't have much to say, as there isn't much to add on, there was lots of story change for our protaginists as I said, but I feel like I am repeating myself alot now. So, time for the game cons.
/// G A M E  C O N S \\\
I can say, from the big wait, that I don't like the series as much as I did because, the hype isn't there anymore. Now that the series has finished, it's so hard to believe, and I'll miss it being around.
But, it was so unsatifying just to see the story end THERE. I understand, fans of Telltale and Telltale themself probally want to move on to finishing their other games to release them, therefore it was a bit subtle. But still, that's just not enough for me, it's just to much of a subtle end.
(BREIF SPOILERS THROUGHOUT THE WHOLE PARAGRAPH!) Near the end of episode 8, you see your "hero" Jesse, going out to see their home town after a huge adventure (with improvements to the town of course, from Axel and Olivia). He/she smiles onto the empty space in the room, and then walks out. You can't just end it like that! I was expecting at least a tiny look around the town, or something else. I just wanted MORE. Of course, that is expected to happen when you are attached to a series, but that story just leaves me empty. There is so much more Telltale could've done with that. I have ideas myself, but I defenitaly cannot produce games myself, I do not have the greatest voice acting either. (I also have difficulty impersonating voices, lol.)
With that, I can say it's likely fan games will come about, continueing the series, which just won't top it off. I'm just not satisfied (which I will accidently continue to repeat) with this ending. I just want a better ending, or maybe more death (hehe). I can see a suprise come back for the game, but that is VERY unlikely. Also, near to the end of episode 8, I saw it was a bit rushed. With the battle scenes very slow paced, slow motion, which means not as much animation being done, which I see as a bit lazy. I mean sure, they have to continue as I mentioned before, but you need to finished what you've started. Sure, I guess similar amounts of animation would be imported even if it was slow, but it still makes me think they had to rush the ending alot, it does make some cool effects though. Anyways, enough about that and more about money..
The fact you have to buy the next few episodes is just rediculous. I saw a review, near to the release of episode 6. It said something like "Do you seriously have to BUY the next few episodes? Oh, people are gonna get really mad thinking 'I bought the Season Pass! Surely I can just play the next few episodes without paying!' but no, you have to pay". These were my exact thoughts seeing that review, you shouldn't have to pay just to play a few more episodes that Telltale made without telling anyone it was coming, if I knew I had to pay, I wouldn't have even bothered to pay for it. I already had the story spoiled for me by watching the series on Youtube, so what's the point?
/// R E V I E W  E N D \\\
This wasn't a decent review, I can tell, but I can say that I do not respect the game as much as I did. I seem a bit repetitive, but I just drilled those thoughts into my mind, had to put it somewhere. Anyways, I still enjoy the game (a bit), and appreciate Tellatale taking their time to make this game. I'd like to apologise to anyone who was affended in this review in anyway. Not because I insulted Telltale, but because I feel like my opinion isn't needed, lol. Eh, otherwise, I will continue to watch out for extra episodes, or a sequel, which as I said, is very unlikely. I'd give it a 3/10, meh..
